.TH HEXAGONRPCD 8 "2025-07" "hexagonrpcd v0.5.0" "System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
hexagonrpcd \- Qualcomm DSP FastRPC reverse tunnel daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBhexagonrpcd\fP [\fIoptions\fP] \fB\-f\fP \fIDEVICE\fP
.SH DESCRIPTION
hexagonrpcd attaches to a Qualcomm Hexagon DSP via the FastRPC kernel driver,
establishes a reverse tunnel for DSP-side RPC calls, and serves file I/O and
memory allocation requests from the DSP. File paths are transparently redirected
through HexagonFS, mapping Android-style paths to configurable Linux paths.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-f \fIDEVICE\fP
FastRPC device node (e.g. /dev/fastrpc-adsp). Required.
.TP
\fB\-c \fIPATH\fP
Create a DSP process domain loading the specified ELF binary (INIT_CREATE).
.TP
\fB\-d \fIDSP\fP
DSP type name for HexagonFS subdirectory (default: empty, e.g. "adsp", "cdsp").
.TP
\fB\-p \fIPROGRAM\fP [\fIargs\fP]
Run client program with shared FastRPC file descriptor.
.TP
\fB\-R \fIDIR\fP
HexagonFS root directory (default: /usr/share/qcom/).
.TP
\fB\-s\fP
Attach to sensors PD (INIT_ATTACH_SNS) instead of root PD.
.SH HEXAGONFS PATH MAPPINGS
DSP file paths are redirected as follows:
.TS
box tab(|);
l|l.
DSP path|Physical path
/vendor/etc/acdbdata/|{root}/acdb/
/vendor/etc/sensors/config/|{root}/sensors/config/
/vendor/etc/sensors/sns_reg_config|{root}/sensors/sns_reg.conf
/persist/sensors/registry/|{root}/sensors/registry/
/sys/devices/soc0/|{root}/socinfo/
/usr/lib/qcom/{dsp}/|{root}/dsp/{dsp}/
.TE
.PP
Hard links: /vendor/ == /system/vendor/, /persist/ == /mnt/vendor/persist/.
.SH FILES
/usr/lib/systemd/system/hexagonrpcd-*.service
/usr/lib/udev/rules.d/60-hexagonrpc.rules
/usr/lib/sysusers.d/hexagonrpc.conf
